      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, intentional. FileMode doesn\u0027t override equals(Object) — it only defines equals(int modeBits). So FileMode.TREE.equals(p.getEntryFileMode()) would bind to Object.equals, i.e. reference equality — the same comparison ReferenceEquality flags on the original !\u003d (it just isn\u0027t flagged because Error Prone doesn\u0027t inspect .equals()).\n\nTo get a genuine value comparison I used the raw-mode int overload: FileMode.TREE.equals(p.getEntryRawMode()). That\u0027s JGit\u0027s own idiom — e.g. BaseSearch (!FileMode.TREE.equals(parser.getEntryRawMode())), and StrategySimpleTwoWayInCore / ResolveMerger / FileModeCache compare tree modes the same way. It\u0027s also more robust than the original, which relied on FileMode instances being interned.\n\nHappy to add a short comment noting the int overload if that helps readability.",
